  "question": {
    "text": "Let a random variable X take values $0,1,2,3$ with $\\mathrm{P}(\\mathrm{X}=0)=\\mathrm{P}(\\mathrm{X}=1)=\\mathrm{p}, \\mathrm{P}(\\mathrm{X}=2)=\\mathrm{P}(\\mathrm{X}=3)$ and $\\mathrm{E}\\left(\\mathrm{X}^2\\right)=2 \\mathrm{E}(\\mathrm{X})$. Then the value of $8 \\mathrm{p}-1$ is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "nIZDP",
      "text": "0",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "zAdSH",
      "text": "2",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "XiTuC",
      "text": "1",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "X0Pjw",
      "text": "3",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & 2 p+2 q=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ & p+q \\\\ & E\\left(x^2\\right)=\\sum_{i=0}^3 x_i^2 p\\left(x_i\\right)=0 \\cdot p+1 \\cdot p+4 \\cdot q+9 q \\\\ & =p+13 q \\\\ & E(x)=\\sum_{i=0}^3 x_i^2 p\\left(x_i\\right)=0 \\cdot p+1 \\cdot p+2 q+3 q=p+5 q \\\\ & p+13 q=2(p+5 q) \\\\ & p=3 q \\\\ & \\text { So, } q=\\frac{1}{8} \\& p=\\frac{3}{8} \\quad \\\\ & \\text { So, } 8 p-1=2 \\quad \\text { Option (2) }\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
